# Files yadm bundles into an ENCRYPTED archive (~/.local/share/yadm/archive),
# which is the only form in which they reach the repo. Patterns are relative
# to $HOME.
#
# Why these are encrypted rather than tracked directly: this dotfiles repo is
# PUBLIC, and Chrome state is real per-context browsing history -- client
# account ids, Boomi component UUIDs, ticket and admin URLs, a personal inbox.
# Individually unremarkable; in aggregate, and permanently in public git
# history, not something to publish by default.
#
# Refresh with `yadm encrypt` (prompts for a passphrase -- symmetric, no GPG
# key needed), then commit the archive. It is DELIBERATELY manual and
# occasional: its only job is surviving a machine migration, which happens
# about once a year, so a debounced automatic write was ~500 writes per event.
#
# On a new machine `yadm decrypt` restores these to their original paths --
# which for Chrome state IS the hot store `context` already reads, so there is
# no import step and no fallback code.
.local/state/context/chrome/*.json
